course: dictionary
lesson: 12547
title: Determine: find out, decide, or settle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Determine» has a few meanings. The most common is to find out something exactly, often by measuring or working it out. «The scientists determined the temperature of the water.» They found the exact number.
explain: It can also mean to decide, or to be the thing that causes a result. «The weather determines whether the match goes ahead.» The rain decides if the match happens. You may also see «be determined to», which means you have made a firm decision, as in «She is determined to win.»
explain: In maths and exams, «Determine» is a command word. «Determine the value of x» means find it, and usually show your working. In everyday talk, people say «work out», «figure out», or «it depends» instead.
fact: Determine means to find out or work out something exactly, often by measuring or calculating.
fact: Determine also means to decide, or to be the thing that causes a result.
fact: «Determined» can mean having made a firm decision to do something, as in «She is determined to finish the race.»
fact: In exams, «Determine» is a command word: it asks you to find an answer and show how you got it.
fact: In casual talk, «work out», «figure out» and «it depends» mean much the same as determine.
exercise: «The scientists determined the temperature of the water.» What does determined mean here? | Forgot all about it | Argued about it | *Found out exactly | Felt very cold
exercise: «The weather determines whether the match goes ahead.» What does determines mean here? | *Decides or controls what will happen | Measures the rain | Makes the players tired | Watches the match
exercise: «She is determined to finish the race.» What does determined mean? | *Firmly decided to do it | Tired and sleepy | Pushed by the crowd | Lost on the way
test: In maths, you see «Determine the value of x.» What does this command ask you to do? | *Find the value of x, and show your working | Ignore x | Guess a number for x | Draw a picture of x
test: Ella says «it depends» means about the same as «determined by». Is that a good everyday swap? | No, it means you must run | *Yes, in casual talk it means roughly the same thing | No, it means the sun is out | No, it means something that is painted
exam: «Determine the total cost of the five tickets.» What must you do? | Guess the total and move on | Write a short story about the tickets | Draw five tickets | *Work out the exact total and show your working
